n carter reed richards and  maria rambo's captain marvel when  america travers and dr strange 616  bursts into their universe and start  looking for the sanctum mordo feign  surprise and delight before taking them  prisoner richards gets strange up to  speed about how the illuminati defeated  their thanos then delivers the bad news  that they've decided that he meaning  every strange variant is the most  dangerous being in the multiverse their  concern isn't unfounded 838 strange used  a dark hold to dreamwalk and killed a  trillion people in an incursion the  illuminati have no doubts they can  handle wonder who they quickly dismiss  their righteous smugness and failure to  listen which is admittedly on brand  taints their characters and it also  makes what comes next frustratingly  predictable  anyone who hope to see more than a few  minutes of the illuminati and dr strange  and the multiverse of madness will have  those hopes viciously dashed once the  scarlet witch arrives read richards who  is supposed to be the smartest man alive  overconfidently stands up to her and  stupidly gives away their secret weapon  he says that black bolt could destroy  her with a single whisper from his mouth  which is all the information wonder  needs to destroy them black bolt's death  is probably the most gruesome in a movie  that contains more than a handful of  brutal and controversial kills wonder  erases his mouth from his face which  panics him into imploding his own brain  she then turns reed into spaghetti cuts  captain carter in half with her own  shield and snaps professor xavier's neck  with her mind even if you don't mind  seeing these characters bite the dust so  easily their deaths are unusually  disturbing by the standards of the mcu  for some fans though it's not the  violence that's the problem but rather  the immediacy with which the illuminati  are dispatched a decision that makes  their inclusion in the plot feel more  like surface level fan service  john krasi