ouls of the  damned who rise in objection to the  sorcerer possessing a dead body poor  christine gets little time to prepare  and no instruction on exactly how to  fight them off which some fans felt  amounted to shoddy writing the scene  does give raymie an opportunity to  sample from his previous work in films  like army of darkness and drag me to  hell but audiences who haven't seen  those movies won't benefit from the  references the result is a sequence that  can be wildly entertaining but also more  than a little confusing  in one of the best exchanges and doctors  strange in the multiverse of madness  wonder calmly argues that it doesn't  seem fair that both she and strange have  broken the rules in the past yes he gets  to remain a hero while she's painted as  a villain the scarlet witch goes on to  do awful unforgivable things but at  least at this moment in time she has a  point it doesn't seem fair though  elizabeth olsen turns in one of the  mcu's strongest performances nailing  both the nuanced intimate moments and  the big evil swings many fans were  surprised and upset by the fact that in  the end wonder isn't redeemed while  strange is the double standard is even  more apparent once we learn that the  finale's evil strange also used the dark  hole to look for universes in which he  ended up with christine granted wonder  does eventually see reason when her  twins from earth 838 appears so  terrified of her she chooses to destroy  mount wondergore and all the darkholds  across the multiverse still wonder's  hard term from avenger to power hungry  multiversal menace has rubbed many  viewers the wrong way specifically some  fans didn't appreciate the way wonder's  plotline seemed to play into toxic  tropes about overly emotional women the  scarlet witch does alternate between  hero and villain in the comics but many  who love the character think elizabeth  olsen's empathetic portrayal is far  better than the subpar stereotypical  writing to which she's